 "limitations": [
  "ANATOMICAL leg only: wiring geometry, NOT an operating point (L164).",
  "Q1 and Q2 are DESCRIPTION: every input to the closed form is stored in l216/static.json and the measured crossing in l217/static.json, so the attribution is arithmetic on stored values and the registration buys a DECISION RULE only (PREREG 0a; L214; Kriegeskorte 2009). Q3 is the only inferential object on this card.",
  "L217 already owns the MEASURED-crossing null and found it degenerate (null_frac_both_cross 0.0505); L230 does not re-pose that contrast, it re-poses it in the closed-form currency.",
  "The closed form and the measurement have DIFFERENT populations: the closed form is defined on 7 of 8 cells (it predicts a crossing beyond d=8 for f4wA|crofts|Ti, which the sweep censors) and undefined on cutwA|crofts|Ti, whose asymptote is negative.",
  "A censored cell has no residual, so its model-adequacy leg is FALSE BY UNMEASURABILITY, never a small residual (L222).",
  "K has two currencies (depth-1 anchor with the shared spectral gap; the stored deep fit with the cell's own r_deep). The branch rests on the anchor, which is the card's own wording; the fit companion is reported and is NOT interchangeable, since it gives the two joints different rates and breaks the shared-rho premise (L218/L227/L229).",
  "d_cf is heavy-tailed in the null (d_cf -> +-inf as K -> 0): no moment of that distribution is admissible, so every read is a rate or a percentile with median/IQR for spread.",
  "The null is a membership permutation inside the handedness class: it relocates L/R labels over the same pool cells with per-side counts held exact. It cannot speak to pool MEMBERSHIP or to any L/R asymmetry in reconstruction completeness.",
  "The two-term model carries ONE rho per substrate x operator; a genuinely two-mode residual appears as a residual failure, which is why PHASE_MODEL_INSUFFICIENT is registered FIRST.",
  "No neuromere column exists on BANC, so no legblock tier is possible."
 ],
 "pins": "ALL GREEN"
